  "languageCode": "eng",
  "text": "Hi Rosa, good to see you again. How have you been since we bumped up your blood pressure medicine? Pretty good, but I've had this dry, tickly cough for about three weeks. It's worse at night. Any fever, or shortness of breath? No fever, and my breathing is fine. And you're taking the lisinopril every day? Yes, every morning. I think it's the 20 milligram, or maybe 40? The bottle's at home. Okay. Your blood pressure today is 138 over 88, which is better than last time. Have you been checking at home? A few times. Mostly in the 130s. Good. That cough is a known side effect of lisinopril, so I'd like to switch you to losartan, 50 milligrams once a day, and stop the lisinopril. Okay, that's fine. Keep cutting back on salt like we discussed. Let's check your blood pressure again in four weeks. Sounds good. Thank you, doctor.",
